\F3 LESSON 4.1 -- REGISTERS AND PUT\F7

Every delete and yank lands in the unnamed register, and p/P paste it:

  p   put after the cursor (charwise) or below the line (linewise)
  P   put before the cursor, or above the line
  "a  prefix: delete or yank into register a ("add, "ayy)
  "A  append to register a. "0 holds the last yank; "1-"9 the delete
      chain. There is no register named by punctuation. vi is orderly.

1. xp: delete the character under the cursor and put it after. Move the
   cursor between the t and the h in ---> and press xp. Undo with u.

---> th is is xp in action.

2. Move a line: dd it, move elsewhere, p it back below the cursor line.

---> I would rather be below the next line.

3. Named registers survive intervening deletes: "ayy a line, delete three
   other lines, then "ap restores the yanked one.

